What:           /sys/devices/platform/.../*.gpu/agx_stats
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        Aurora Silicon developers
Description:
                Read-only, per-device firmware GPU utilization on T8140 G17P.
                With asahi.stats_export=0, the file reports unsupported.
                The default value 1 enables the version 2 export described here.
                Earlier GPU generations use the separate legacy agx_stats format.
                Version 2 is a whitespace-delimited key/value format. Readers
                must check the version and load_valid before using percentages.

                version: 2
                source: firmware
                load_valid: 1 if the current utilization is available, else 0
                busy_percent: firmware aggregate utilization, percent (0..100)
                util1..util3: firmware engine percentages (0..100); engine labels
                             are not assigned without independent validation
                util4: same aggregate as busy_percent; do not sum engine values
                gpu_power_known: whether a timestamped power state was received
                gpu_powered: 0 when firmware reports the GPU powered off, else 1
                samples: accepted primary utilization reports since probe
                sample_received_ns: host CLOCK_MONOTONIC receive timestamp
                sample_age_ns: time since the retained utilization report
                sample_timestamp_ticks: 64-bit firmware utilization timestamp
                power_timestamp_ticks: newest secondary power-state timestamp
                clock_hz: 24000000 (timestamp and residency ticks)
                powered_ticks: completed powered intervals, accumulated from
                               firmware power-off records since probe
                unpowered_ticks: completed unpowered intervals, accumulated from
                                 firmware power-on records since probe
                invalid_samples: malformed utilization/power records rejected

                A timestamped power-off witness overrides retained utilization
                with zero. After wake, an old utilization report is unavailable
                until a report for the new interval arrives. Device loss or
                shutdown invalidates load until a new device is probed. Receive timestamps
                do not order events across firmware rings: firmware timestamps
                determine which state is newer. Suspend can separate the host
                and firmware clocks; do not subtract values from those domains.

                Power residency is not GPU busy time. Residency counters omit
                the currently open power interval and saturate at U64_MAX.
                Neither these counters nor the percentages are per-client DRM
                engine execution time. No per-client execution counter is
                synthesized from queue admission, wall time or job spans.

                Reading debugfs asahi-g17/statistics requests two seconds of full
                raw-payload capture, including undecoded record kinds. Repeat
                reads to keep diagnostic capture active. It is disabled by
                default and is not needed for normal utilization reporting.
                Trace records and uncaptured statistics only read required words.
                Captured counts exclude records outside the capture window. That diagnostic format is not a
                stable userspace ABI. Optional telemetry registration failure
                does not prevent GPU initialization and is logged by the driver.
